Description: ignore the multi-byte enum derive tests, they exercise undefined behaviour
 The derived Endian impl for an integer-repr enum transmutes the byte-swapped
 discriminant back into the enum type. For a multi-byte repr the swapped value
 (e.g. 16 -> 0x1000) is not a valid discriminant, which is undefined behaviour.
 Since the debug-mode enum discriminant check in recent rustc (seen with
 1.94.1), the test binary aborts with "panic_invalid_enum_construction":
 to_be() trips it on little-endian hosts, to_le() on big-endian ones (s390x).
 The 8-bit test (no swap) and all struct tests keep running. No Proxmox crate
 derives Endian on an enum.
